# The goldens are compared byte for byte (tests/goldens.py), so the bytes in the working
# tree must be the bytes that were written.  Git on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout by default; `eol=lf` pins the checkout on every platform.  The comparison reads
# with universal newlines as well, so a checkout that ignores this file still passes.
tests/golden/** text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/** text eol=lf
